{"The lazy initialization `@loaded_locales ||= []` is not protected by `LOAD_MUTEX`, unlike every other mutation of `@loaded_locales` in this class. In a multi-threaded server this can race with `reload!`, which resets `@loaded_locales` and `@cache` in sequence. Wrapping the check-and-load inside `LOAD_MUTEX.synchronize` (similar to `load_locale`) would make this safe.": 0.8623968362808228, "The `locale` parameter is not normalized (e.g., via `.to_sym`), so passing `\"en\"` vs `:en` would bypass the `include?` guard and load the same locale twice. The existing `translate` method always uses `config.locale` (a symbol), but `ensure_loaded!` is a new public entry point with no such guarantee.": 0.6547057032585144}